# Docker build-context exclusions for the frontend image
# (frontend/Dockerfile, context: frontend/). This is not just hygiene --
# frontend/Dockerfile uses `COPY . .`, so without this file a host-local
# `node_modules/` (with platform-specific native binaries, e.g. built on
# Windows/macOS) would be copied into the Linux container image and could
# silently break the runtime. See docs/IMPLEMENTATION-ROADMAP.md Phase 1.4.

node_modules
.next
.turbo
out
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets -- never sent to the Docker build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# VCS / editor
.git
.vscode
.idea
*.log
